WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.070
My name is Yuma Tsukumo!

00:00:02.070 --> 00:00:03.850
My goal is to become
the dueling champion!

00:00:03.850 --> 00:00:07.820
Retrieve the Numbers! They’re my memories!

00:00:07.820 --> 00:00:09.110
Be quiet!

00:00:09.110 --> 00:00:11.710
There’s big trouble in my city!

00:00:11.710 --> 00:00:13.980
There’s a computer virus bomb!

00:00:13.980 --> 00:00:16.160
If it explodes,
the city will be in a panic!

00:00:16.160 --> 00:00:19.440
The culprit is my teacher!

00:00:19.440 --> 00:00:22.120
I have to win the duel
and stop the virus bomb!

00:00:22.520 --> 00:00:25.170
I’m kattobing!

00:00:29.210 --> 00:00:32.470
I set one card.

00:00:32.470 --> 00:00:33.690
I end my turn.

00:00:36.690 --> 00:00:38.180
Damn!

00:00:38.180 --> 00:00:40.770
How dare you use my monster!

00:00:40.770 --> 00:00:44.150
The virus bomb will
activate in 20 minutes.

00:00:44.730 --> 00:00:46.220
My turn!

00:00:46.830 --> 00:00:48.690
It’s my turn!

00:00:48.690 --> 00:00:52.700
Is Yuma still talking to himself?

00:00:52.700 --> 00:00:54.700
To summarize, is he okay?

00:00:54.700 --> 00:00:57.200
He’s fine. Don’t worry about it.

00:00:57.840 --> 00:01:00.620
That’s Yuma in kattobing mode.

00:01:02.120 --> 00:01:04.120
My turn! I draw!

00:01:04.120 --> 00:01:07.080
Yuma, summon Ganbara Knight.

00:01:07.080 --> 00:01:09.390
Stop butting in!

00:01:09.390 --> 00:01:12.300
There’s a Number
at risk in this duel.

00:01:12.300 --> 00:01:16.300
If he takes my
Number, I’ll vanish.

00:01:16.760 --> 00:01:19.220
I don’t care about you!

00:01:19.220 --> 00:01:21.230
You can’t win on your own.

00:01:21.840 --> 00:01:23.390
What?

00:01:23.390 --> 00:01:25.940
If you’re gonna say that,
I made up my mind!

00:01:25.940 --> 00:01:29.400
I won’t listen
to you during this duel!

00:01:29.400 --> 00:01:32.550
Won’t listen? What do you mean?

00:01:32.550 --> 00:01:36.230
If you say right,
I’m going left.

00:01:36.230 --> 00:01:39.030
If you tell me to
summon Ganbara Knight...

00:01:39.030 --> 00:01:41.780
I summon Achacha Archer!

00:01:45.890 --> 00:01:46.910
What?

00:01:46.910 --> 00:01:52.750
When I successfully summon this card,
you take 500 points of damage!

00:02:00.390 --> 00:02:01.940
How’s that!

00:02:01.940 --> 00:02:04.390
I dealt damage to my teacher!

00:02:04.390 --> 00:02:06.390
But it came
at a high price.

00:02:07.600 --> 00:02:12.150
If you summoned Ganbara Knight,
you would’ve had two Level 4 monsters.

00:02:12.150 --> 00:02:15.490
You could’ve Xyz Summoned Utopia.

00:02:16.020 --> 00:02:17.950
Oh yeah! I forgot!

00:02:19.320 --> 00:02:21.490
I knew about that!

00:02:21.490 --> 00:02:24.760
How dare you damage
my LP!

00:02:25.200 --> 00:02:29.830
I activate the trap card
Damage Vaccine Ω MAX!

00:02:29.830 --> 00:02:36.300
When I take damage, I regain LP
equal to the damage I took.

00:02:37.060 --> 00:02:39.630
That means my attack was pointless!

00:02:39.630 --> 00:02:42.970
I’m aiming for perfect victory!

00:02:42.970 --> 00:02:45.600
I won’t let you
damage my life points!

00:02:47.560 --> 00:02:50.250
This is bad!

00:02:50.250 --> 00:02:54.730
Even though I was used,
I sent the virus bomb!

00:02:54.730 --> 00:02:57.990
To summarize, I’ll also
be treated as a criminal!

00:02:57.990 --> 00:03:01.560
There’s no time left, Yuma...

00:03:05.620 --> 00:03:08.700
Whether it’s rain, wind,
blizzard or the scorching sun

00:03:08.700 --> 00:03:11.830
They give color to each day
Will and love keep me from losing heart

00:03:11.830 --> 00:03:14.880
Your kindness was harsh
I learned frustration when we clashed

00:03:14.880 --> 00:03:19.010
Freedom begins by accepting differences
Dance and create the universe

00:03:21.180 --> 00:03:26.390
In truth, I was sad
until I met you

00:03:27.310 --> 00:03:33.040
I lied, thinking it was
easier to be alone

00:03:33.040 --> 00:03:39.490
Even though we don’t like
the same books or hobbies

00:03:39.490 --> 00:03:43.360
You’re the only one
who agreed with me

00:03:43.360 --> 00:03:46.490
Joy and sadness and anger
and do re mi fa so la ti do

00:03:46.490 --> 00:03:48.490
There’s no harmony and scenario
without differences

00:03:49.160 --> 00:03:51.580
Everyone is not the same

00:03:52.500 --> 00:03:56.590
That’s the reason for living

00:03:56.590 --> 00:04:01.840
Even if the sounds
are dissonant at times

00:04:01.840 --> 00:04:07.260
That’s why I never give up
I believe my strength will get me through

00:04:08.310 --> 00:04:11.320
I travel to
the edge of the world

00:04:11.320 --> 00:04:14.980
The sights I see
with you are the truth

00:04:14.980 --> 00:04:17.820
Whether it’s rain, wind,
blizzard or the scorching sun

00:04:17.820 --> 00:04:21.360
They give color to each day
Will and love keep me from losing heart

00:04:21.400 --> 00:04:24.450
Your kindness was harsh
I learned frustration when we clashed

00:04:24.450 --> 00:04:28.580
Freedom begins by accepting differences
Dance and create the universe

00:04:33.710 --> 00:04:38.630
Countdown to a Comeback! Astral is the Secret Plan?!

00:04:33.710 --> 00:04:38.630
Number 4:

00:04:33.710 --> 00:04:38.630
Countdown to a Comeback! Astral is the Secret Plan?!

00:04:35.550 --> 00:04:38.630
The virus bomb switch should be up ahead.

00:04:38.630 --> 00:04:40.530
I’ll stop it!

00:04:41.510 --> 00:04:44.470
I end my turn!

00:04:44.470 --> 00:04:47.330
My turn! I draw!

00:04:47.330 --> 00:04:52.200
I activate Number 34: Terror-Byte’s effect!

00:04:52.200 --> 00:04:59.620
Once per turn, I can use an Overlay Unit
to take control of your Level 4-or-below monster.

00:05:00.290 --> 00:05:02.810
My Gogogo Golem again!

00:05:03.360 --> 00:05:08.690
If you summoned Utopia,
he couldn’t have taken control of it.

00:05:09.330 --> 00:05:14.290
Terror-Byte’s effect takes control
of a monster with a Level.

00:05:14.850 --> 00:05:19.000
However, Xyz Monsters don’t have Levels.

00:05:20.060 --> 00:05:21.920
Your dueling is incomplete.

00:05:21.920 --> 00:05:23.310
You should obey me.

00:05:23.310 --> 00:05:25.130
Be quiet!

00:05:25.130 --> 00:05:30.850
I’ll take damage, but Gogogo
Golem will return to my field.

00:05:30.850 --> 00:05:32.260
When that happens...

00:05:33.520 --> 00:05:38.630
I’m not a foolish duelist who uses
the same strategy as the previous turn.

00:05:38.630 --> 00:05:42.530
I activate the Continuous Spells
Infected Mail and Cracking!

00:05:43.460 --> 00:05:45.490
What’s a Continuous Spell?

00:05:46.240 --> 00:05:52.870
Unlike a Normal Spell Card, a Continuous Spell’s effect
continues as long as the card remains on the field.

00:05:53.710 --> 00:06:00.820
Due to Infected Mail’s effect, a Level 4-or-below
monster can attack you directly once per turn.

00:06:00.820 --> 00:06:04.010
Afterwards, that monster is destroyed.

00:06:04.010 --> 00:06:05.090
That means...

00:06:05.090 --> 00:06:09.160
Go, Gogogo Golem! Attack him directly!

00:06:17.640 --> 00:06:22.580
Due to Infected Mail’s effect,
Gogogo Golem is destroyed after battle!

00:06:25.370 --> 00:06:27.280
Gogogo Golem!

00:06:27.280 --> 00:06:32.530
Now the other Continuous Spell
Cracking’s effect activates!

00:06:32.980 --> 00:06:40.000
When your monster is destroyed and sent to the graveyard,
you take 800 points of damage!

00:06:41.820 --> 00:06:43.500
Did you see that?

00:06:43.500 --> 00:06:46.670
This is my Terror-Byte combo.

00:06:46.670 --> 00:06:47.850
Damn!

00:06:47.850 --> 00:06:51.650
I have to do something
about his Terror-Byte combo or I’m done!

00:06:53.050 --> 00:06:54.120
Huh?

00:06:55.390 --> 00:06:58.760
Is your body fading?

00:06:59.670 --> 00:07:03.800
When you lose LP,
I also lose my life.

00:07:04.230 --> 00:07:07.030
Your life?

00:07:07.070 --> 00:07:10.950
If I fail,
I’ll lose many things.

00:07:11.540 --> 00:07:13.440
What’s wrong with Yuma?

00:07:13.440 --> 00:07:14.600
He doesn’t seem happy.

00:07:14.600 --> 00:07:16.380
That’s bad!

00:07:16.380 --> 00:07:19.150
I have to do something!

00:07:19.800 --> 00:07:20.580
I know!

00:07:20.580 --> 00:07:22.210
Yuma!

00:07:22.580 --> 00:07:27.760
Yuma, you’re “Garyu! Housuu!”

00:07:29.310 --> 00:07:30.680
Gachon broadcast?

00:07:30.680 --> 00:07:32.090
No!

00:07:32.500 --> 00:07:34.900
Garyu is a sleeping dragon.

00:07:34.900 --> 00:07:38.100
And housuu is a juvenile phoenix!

00:07:38.100 --> 00:07:42.100
To summarize, it means tremendous
talent sleeps within you!

00:07:42.100 --> 00:07:43.760
Me?

00:07:43.760 --> 00:07:47.780
If that talent awakens,
you will definitely win!

00:07:48.690 --> 00:07:51.490
That’s a lot of praise!

00:07:51.490 --> 00:07:54.920
All right! I’ll try my best!

00:07:55.620 --> 00:08:00.580
Observation #6: When humans
receive praise, they try harder.

00:08:01.710 --> 00:08:05.370
Yuma, there’s something
I want to talk to you about.

00:08:05.370 --> 00:08:06.090
What is it?

00:08:06.090 --> 00:08:10.210
You have a continuous combo
where you eat and emit.

00:08:10.210 --> 00:08:14.170
You can’t jump over the vaulting boxes
and cause panic at the pool.

00:08:14.170 --> 00:08:16.180
You’re also stubborn and weird.

00:08:17.090 --> 00:08:18.430
To summarize...

00:08:19.380 --> 00:08:20.890
You are incredible.

00:08:20.890 --> 00:08:24.320
Are you picking
a fight with me?

00:08:26.440 --> 00:08:27.400
What is it?

00:08:28.650 --> 00:08:30.940
The room is moving?

00:08:38.010 --> 00:08:40.660
We’re outside!

00:08:41.700 --> 00:08:43.330
It’s still rising!

00:08:46.390 --> 00:08:47.670
I did it!

00:08:47.670 --> 00:08:49.630
The door to the final section!

00:08:57.430 --> 00:09:00.140
Fine, I’ll fight you!

00:09:03.850 --> 00:09:07.570
Don’t underestimate a karate black belt!

00:09:12.680 --> 00:09:16.970
This is the best seat to see
the results of the virus bomb.

00:09:19.530 --> 00:09:23.210
I set one card
and end my turn.

00:09:23.210 --> 00:09:27.040
Damn! What happened to you, teacher?

00:09:27.570 --> 00:09:29.770
Yuma will lose.

00:09:29.770 --> 00:09:33.010
But I must win.

00:09:33.370 --> 00:09:35.840
I won’t listen
to you during this duel!

00:09:35.840 --> 00:09:39.930
If you say right,
I’m going left.

00:09:39.930 --> 00:09:41.350
There is a way.

00:09:41.890 --> 00:09:42.930
Here I go!

00:09:42.930 --> 00:09:45.230
My turn! I draw!

00:09:45.230 --> 00:09:48.150
All right! I drew
a good card!

00:09:48.150 --> 00:09:51.320
I summon Goblindbergh!

00:09:53.900 --> 00:09:55.140
All right!

00:09:55.140 --> 00:09:58.320
To summarize, when Goblindbergh
is successfully summoned...

00:09:58.750 --> 00:10:02.830
...he can Special Summon
a Level 4-or-below monster from his hand!

00:10:02.830 --> 00:10:05.180
Yuma, summon Zubaba Knight
from your hand!

00:10:05.180 --> 00:10:06.820
I don’t want to!

00:10:06.820 --> 00:10:08.790
If you say Zubaba Knight...

00:10:09.920 --> 00:10:15.080
I Special Summon Ganbara Knight!

00:10:17.270 --> 00:10:21.410
I have Level 4 Ganbara Knight
and Goblindbergh on my field.

00:10:21.410 --> 00:10:22.260
That means...

00:10:22.260 --> 00:10:25.270
I can Xyz Summon Utopia!

00:10:26.770 --> 00:10:29.230
I’m kattobing!

00:10:29.230 --> 00:10:33.890
I overlay Level 4 Ganbara Knight
and Goblindbergh!

00:10:35.490 --> 00:10:39.190
With these two monsters,
I build the Overlay Network!

00:10:39.860 --> 00:10:41.610
Xyz Summon!

00:10:43.240 --> 00:10:47.410
Appear, Number 39: Utopia!

00:10:55.780 --> 00:10:57.940
I’m counting on you, Utopia!

00:11:02.110 --> 00:11:07.640
Number 39: Utopia.

00:11:08.380 --> 00:11:11.360
Yuma, don’t set a trap
from your hand.

00:11:11.360 --> 00:11:13.430
You’re not good
enough to use it.

00:11:13.430 --> 00:11:14.400
Be quiet!

00:11:14.400 --> 00:11:18.690
I said that I won’t
follow your directions!

00:11:18.690 --> 00:11:22.160
I set one card
and end my turn!

00:11:24.270 --> 00:11:26.660
How dare you erase my article!

00:11:26.740 --> 00:11:29.330
Take this and this and this!

00:11:31.830 --> 00:11:33.290
I did it!

00:11:36.880 --> 00:11:39.800
My turn! I draw!

00:11:39.800 --> 00:11:42.000
I activate Terror-Byte’s effect!

00:11:42.840 --> 00:11:47.840
By using an Overlay Unit,
I take control of Achacha Archer!

00:11:51.050 --> 00:11:52.850
He took my monster again.

00:11:52.850 --> 00:12:00.070
Due to the Continuous Spell Infected Mail’s effect,
Achacha Archer will be destroyed after it attacks you directly!

00:12:00.070 --> 00:12:03.320
To summarize, Yuma will lose!

00:12:04.790 --> 00:12:07.430
Isn’t there a way
to dodge it?

00:12:08.080 --> 00:12:12.040
Utopia doesn’t have
such a convenient effect.

00:12:12.040 --> 00:12:13.820
Utopia’s effect...

00:12:14.620 --> 00:12:15.500
Oh yeah!

00:12:15.500 --> 00:12:18.110
I activate Utopia’s effect!

00:12:18.110 --> 00:12:20.380
I use an Overlay Unit!

00:12:24.390 --> 00:12:27.690
I negate one monster’s attack!

00:12:28.560 --> 00:12:33.690
Infected Mail’s effect only activates
if the direct attack succeeds.

00:12:34.340 --> 00:12:38.650
Since Utopia’s effect negated the attack,
it doesn’t go to the graveyard.

00:12:39.420 --> 00:12:42.320
Cracking’s effect also doesn’t activate.

00:12:42.320 --> 00:12:45.870
I see! I can stop
my teacher’s combo!

00:12:47.020 --> 00:12:49.290
It seems I underestimated you.

00:12:49.290 --> 00:12:52.820
Yuma is unexpectedly intelligent.

00:12:52.820 --> 00:12:55.920
To summarize, is it
because of the ghost duelist?

00:12:55.920 --> 00:12:57.420
Ghost duelist?

00:12:57.420 --> 00:13:00.950
He used up all
his Overlay Units.

00:13:00.950 --> 00:13:03.590
Yeah! He can no longer
use his Terror-Byte combo!

00:13:03.590 --> 00:13:08.520
Did you think that
I didn’t expect your strategy?

00:13:08.520 --> 00:13:09.490
What?

00:13:09.490 --> 00:13:13.450
The conditions for my perfect
victory have now been met.

00:13:13.450 --> 00:13:16.180
I activate the trap Bug Switch!

00:13:17.730 --> 00:13:22.480
When Crashbug X,
Y and Z are in my graveyard...

00:13:22.480 --> 00:13:29.540
I can switch my monster from attack to defense position
to Special Summon Super Crashbug in face-up defense position!

00:13:30.950 --> 00:13:33.030
Phew.

00:13:33.030 --> 00:13:36.420
I thought that monster would attack,
but it’s in defense position.

00:13:36.420 --> 00:13:40.340
Do you think I would do
something so pointless?

00:13:40.340 --> 00:13:43.310
I activate Super Crashbug’s effect!

00:13:43.310 --> 00:13:49.550
When this card is face-up, monsters in attack
position swap their ATK and DEF.

00:13:50.130 --> 00:13:52.860
Terror-Byte has 2900 DEF.

00:13:52.860 --> 00:13:56.020
Therefore, Terror-Byte’s ATK becomes 2900!

00:13:57.220 --> 00:13:59.980
2900 ATK?

00:13:59.980 --> 00:14:03.820
And Utopia and Archer’s ATK...

00:14:03.820 --> 00:14:06.310
I attack!

00:14:06.310 --> 00:14:07.780
Go, Terror-Byte!

00:14:08.280 --> 00:14:10.280
Attack Utopia!

00:14:10.280 --> 00:14:11.280
Don’t dodge!

00:14:11.280 --> 00:14:13.270
Of course I’ll dodge it!

00:14:13.270 --> 00:14:15.500
I activate Utopia’s effect!

00:14:15.500 --> 00:14:20.130
I use an Overlay Unit
to negate one monster’s attack!

00:14:22.110 --> 00:14:23.390
He did it!

00:14:23.390 --> 00:14:25.120
This is bad!

00:14:25.120 --> 00:14:30.430
Utopia used up all of its Overlay Units,
so Yuma can no longer prevent any attacks!

00:14:30.430 --> 00:14:33.850
I set one card
and end my turn!

00:14:36.330 --> 00:14:38.390
That set card is...

00:14:38.390 --> 00:14:42.650
It’ll be over
on my next turn.

00:14:44.440 --> 00:14:46.900
My turn! I draw!

00:14:46.900 --> 00:14:50.240
Terror-Byte has 2900 ATK.

00:14:50.240 --> 00:14:53.870
If I don’t beat my teacher this turn,
Utopia will be destroyed.

00:14:53.870 --> 00:14:56.160
I’ll give you one tip.

00:14:56.160 --> 00:15:04.090
Don’t use Zubaba Knight and Achacha Archer
to Xyz Summon Leviathan Dragon.

00:15:04.090 --> 00:15:08.920
Oh yeah! I have another Number!

00:15:09.720 --> 00:15:12.710
I summon Zubaba Knight!

00:15:18.940 --> 00:15:21.130
I’m kattobing!

00:15:21.130 --> 00:15:26.120
I overlay Level 3 Zubaba Knight
and Achacha Archer!

00:15:26.120 --> 00:15:29.690
I use these two monsters
to build the Overlay Network!

00:15:29.690 --> 00:15:31.140
Xyz Summon!

00:15:32.660 --> 00:15:35.650
Appear, Number 17!

00:15:37.080 --> 00:15:39.080
Leviathan Dragon!

00:15:40.650 --> 00:15:42.360
A second Number.

00:15:42.360 --> 00:15:45.920
But you forgot about
Super Crashbug’s effect.

00:15:46.470 --> 00:15:52.180
When Super Crashbug is on the field,
monsters in attack position swap their ATK and DEF.

00:15:52.180 --> 00:15:54.830
Leviathan Dragon has 0 DEF!

00:15:54.830 --> 00:15:57.430
Therefore, its ATK becomes 0!

00:15:58.390 --> 00:16:01.170
I worked hard to
summon Leviathan Dragon!

00:16:01.170 --> 00:16:03.400
It’s because you’re
giving me unwanted advice!

00:16:03.790 --> 00:16:05.610
Like telling me not to dodge!

00:16:05.610 --> 00:16:07.720
If I didn’t dodge—

00:16:09.040 --> 00:16:10.280
Don’t dodge!

00:16:10.700 --> 00:16:13.240
He wouldn’t say something so foolish.

00:16:13.240 --> 00:16:16.780
If you say right,
I’m going left.

00:16:17.180 --> 00:16:19.760
Were you doing that on purpose?

00:16:19.760 --> 00:16:23.000
Yuma, activate Thunder Short
from your hand.

00:16:23.410 --> 00:16:25.910
If you use it, you’ll win.

00:16:27.030 --> 00:16:28.610
I’m not lying.

00:16:29.010 --> 00:16:32.470
If you don’t do it,
I’ll vanish from this world.

00:16:34.890 --> 00:16:38.930
I activate the spell card
Thunder Short from my hand!

00:16:39.620 --> 00:16:44.460
You take 500 points of damage
for every monster you have.

00:16:44.460 --> 00:16:47.370
You take 1000 points of damage!

00:16:49.500 --> 00:16:51.400
You’re resisting in vain!

00:16:51.920 --> 00:16:55.870
I activate Damage
Vaccine Ω MAX again!

00:16:55.870 --> 00:17:01.580
When I take damage, I regain LP
equal to the damage I took!

00:17:01.580 --> 00:17:04.290
It was pointless!

00:17:04.290 --> 00:17:06.750
Yuma, the trap card.

00:17:07.430 --> 00:17:08.990
Trap card?

00:17:09.410 --> 00:17:13.720
Oh yeah! I activate
the trap card Overconfidence!

00:17:13.720 --> 00:17:15.430
What?

00:17:15.430 --> 00:17:22.220
When you regain LP,
one monster on your field is destroyed!

00:17:22.220 --> 00:17:25.690
I destroy Super Crashbug!

00:17:27.520 --> 00:17:28.960
Well done!

00:17:28.960 --> 00:17:36.410
To summarize, Super Crashbug’s effect vanishes,
so the monsters’ ATK and DEF are no longer swapped!

00:17:37.120 --> 00:17:38.610
Oh no!

00:17:38.610 --> 00:17:40.870
Terror-Byte has 0 ATK!

00:17:41.370 --> 00:17:43.580
Go, Leviathan Dragon!

00:17:43.580 --> 00:17:46.330
Attack Terror-Byte!

00:17:55.220 --> 00:17:58.680
Next, Utopia attacks you directly!

00:17:58.680 --> 00:18:00.720
Go!

00:18:01.660 --> 00:18:03.930
Hope Sword Slash!

00:18:11.270 --> 00:18:13.900
Hooray! Yuma won!

00:18:13.900 --> 00:18:16.040
It’s a miraculous come-from-behind victory!

00:18:17.570 --> 00:18:19.240
I won!

00:18:19.240 --> 00:18:22.220
I won kattobing!

00:18:22.660 --> 00:18:24.850
You managed to win.

00:18:25.570 --> 00:18:30.120
How did you know my teacher
was going to restore his LP?

00:18:30.120 --> 00:18:32.380
Because he was aiming for perfection.

00:18:33.830 --> 00:18:37.510
During the duel,
he always aimed for perfection.

00:18:38.060 --> 00:18:44.750
I knew that if he took damage from Thunder Short,
he’d definitely try to restore his LP.

00:18:56.200 --> 00:18:59.530
This card is one of
my missing memories.

00:19:00.180 --> 00:19:04.350
Number 34 is
a piece of my memories.

00:19:08.030 --> 00:19:09.900
My name is Astral.

00:19:12.090 --> 00:19:16.460
I came from Astral World.

00:19:20.880 --> 00:19:23.430
My mission in this world is...

00:19:23.430 --> 00:19:25.120
Teacher!

00:19:25.120 --> 00:19:28.020
Teacher!

00:19:28.510 --> 00:19:30.390
What happened to me?

00:19:30.930 --> 00:19:34.570
Teacher! Hurry up
and stop the virus bomb!

00:19:34.570 --> 00:19:35.860
Virus bomb?

00:19:36.420 --> 00:19:39.040
It can’t be stopped.

00:19:39.040 --> 00:19:40.320
It doesn’t have a cancellation switch.

00:19:40.320 --> 00:19:42.200
What?

00:19:42.200 --> 00:19:43.810
Then the city will be...

00:19:44.830 --> 00:19:47.740
Stop being annoying!

00:19:49.940 --> 00:19:51.280
I did it!

00:19:53.180 --> 00:19:54.670
The timer isn’t stopping!

00:19:54.670 --> 00:19:58.050
3...2...1...

00:20:02.470 --> 00:20:04.470
The city will be
in a huge panic!

00:20:04.470 --> 00:20:06.010
It’s all over!

00:20:06.010 --> 00:20:08.670
Huge panic? What do you mean?

00:20:08.670 --> 00:20:13.190
Teacher, you rewrote the city’s programs
to cause a huge panic!

00:20:13.190 --> 00:20:15.690
Why would I do such a
terrifying thing?

00:20:15.690 --> 00:20:18.140
Nothing is happening.

00:20:18.140 --> 00:20:23.260
It’s true that while I was getting ready,
I caused unexpected trouble in the city.

00:20:23.260 --> 00:20:27.010
Then what were you planning to do
with the virus bomb?

00:20:28.000 --> 00:20:29.080
All right, it’s lit!

00:20:29.080 --> 00:20:30.980
It’s now complete!

00:20:30.980 --> 00:20:33.540
Everyone, look at the sky
with your D-Gazers.

00:20:33.540 --> 00:20:36.590
Look at the sky
with my D-Gazer?

00:20:39.880 --> 00:20:41.630
Is that Crashbug?

00:20:42.970 --> 00:20:45.820
It’s a gigantic Crashbug!

00:20:46.350 --> 00:20:53.070
I noticed that this city’s night
lights randomly drew a matrix code.

00:20:53.990 --> 00:20:58.140
The D-Gazer reacts to it,
making Crashbug appear!

00:20:58.540 --> 00:21:04.740
But the code was incomplete
because that building wasn’t lit.

00:21:04.740 --> 00:21:10.680
Your perfection was to turn
on that building’s lights?

00:21:10.680 --> 00:21:11.690
Yes.

00:21:12.580 --> 00:21:14.500
Teacher!

00:21:14.500 --> 00:21:16.290
Here, Yuma.

00:21:17.630 --> 00:21:20.490
This is a Crashbug card.

00:21:20.980 --> 00:21:22.010
Read the text.

00:21:23.650 --> 00:21:25.020
It’s Crashbug!

00:21:25.020 --> 00:21:26.350
It’s cute!

00:21:26.350 --> 00:21:28.220
Crashbug!

00:21:28.220 --> 00:21:32.010
I didn’t make it in time,
but nothing happened.

00:21:32.770 --> 00:21:36.960
Crashbug is an electric fairy
that eats people’s bugs.

00:21:36.960 --> 00:21:39.960
When it eats too many bugs,
it becomes gigantic.

00:21:39.960 --> 00:21:45.930
If you see it under a full moon,
you’ll have a wonderful life.

00:21:45.930 --> 00:21:49.950
To summarize, our teacher
wanted to make everyone happy.

00:21:52.130 --> 00:21:53.870
Observation #7:

00:21:54.660 --> 00:22:03.970
If a person touches a Number card, which is a piece of my memories, his heart’s desires and darkness are magnified.

00:22:04.510 --> 00:22:06.720
I’ll remember that.

00:22:13.100 --> 00:22:15.300
Let’s start the duel!

00:22:16.120 --> 00:22:17.720
This week’s quiz:

00:22:17.720 --> 00:22:21.960
When a monster is in attack
position, it’s vertical.

00:22:21.960 --> 00:22:24.820
What if it’s in defense position?

00:22:30.030 --> 00:22:34.980
Today’s test is hard
Can’t avoid pleasure and temptation

00:22:34.980 --> 00:22:39.880
I want to go home and watch TV
Recent cartoons are entertaining

00:22:49.800 --> 00:22:54.600
Anyway, tests are hard
Language, math and English are especially hard

00:22:54.600 --> 00:22:59.480
Average scores in science and social studies
I’m only good at P.E.

00:22:59.480 --> 00:23:02.480
(Wait, Baby!) The expected

00:23:02.480 --> 00:23:04.780
(What’s that, Baby!) Answers

00:23:04.780 --> 00:23:07.480
(Wait a sec, Baby!) Remember them

00:23:07.480 --> 00:23:08.820
(What are we!? Baby!) For who

00:23:08.820 --> 00:23:13.780
Let’s say I wrote
the correct answers on that sheet

00:23:13.780 --> 00:23:18.040
Will that change the future a year
or a decade from now?

00:23:18.630 --> 00:23:23.740
The world I drew
at the edge of dreams

00:23:23.740 --> 00:23:28.720
Someday I’ll race in the sky

00:23:28.720 --> 00:23:33.220
Nobody can threaten my heart

00:23:33.300 --> 00:23:37.320
Nothing is correct!

00:23:41.270 --> 00:23:44.700
What? You’re giving me
an Xyz Monster?

00:23:44.700 --> 00:23:45.900
You can’t take it, Yuma!

00:23:45.900 --> 00:23:47.550
He’s hiding something!

00:23:47.550 --> 00:23:49.860
It’s dangerous to duel him.

00:23:49.860 --> 00:23:52.150
Be quiet! He’s not like that!

00:23:52.530 --> 00:23:54.240
Ante rule?

00:23:54.240 --> 00:23:56.120
For a Number?

00:23:57.120 --> 00:23:58.040
Utopia!

00:23:58.040 --> 00:24:01.160
Why, Tokunosuke?

00:24:01.960 --> 00:24:05.670
Next time on Yu-Gi-Oh! ZEXAL:
“Outwit the Duel!”

00:24:03.670 --> 00:24:09.970
Outwit the Duel!

00:24:05.670 --> 00:24:08.670
I’m kattobing!

00:24:11.610 --> 00:24:15.000
Defense position... is horizontal!

00:24:15.000 --> 00:24:19.300
It’s important during a duel whether a monster
is in attack position or defense position!
